    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0162",
      "reading_order": 216,
      "section": "Water drains",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 255.30099999999993,
        "r": 531.8232999999996,
        "b": 216.72400000000005
      },
      "content": "The compressors have an electronic water drain (EWD). The condensate from the air cooler accumulates in a collector. When the condensate reaches a certain level, it is discharged through the automatic drain outlet (Da)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0163",
      "reading_order": 217,
      "section": "Water drains",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 209.76099999999997,
        "r": 519.8057999999991,
        "b": 184.38400000000001
      },
      "content": "On Full-Feature compressors, an additional electronic water drain (EWD1) is provided. The condensate trap of the heat exchanger is drained by EWD1 and discharged through automatic drain outlet (Da1)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0164",
      "reading_order": 218,
      "section": "Water drains",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 177.42100000000005,
        "r": 534.0694999999994,
        "b": 152.0440000000001
      },
      "content": "Also see section Air flow. Testing the electronic water drain can be done by briefly pressing the test button (1) on top of the drain."
    }
  ]
